---
export const prerender = false;

import HelpLayout from '@/layouts/HelpLayout.astro';
---

<HelpLayout
  title="Badges - DRepTalk"
  description="How achievement badges work on DRepTalk: earned automatically from on-chain and forum activity, with bronze, silver, and gold tiers and a few hidden surprises."
  crumb="Badges"
>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:60ch;line-height:1.6;">
    Badges recognize governance participation. They are earned automatically; there is
    nothing to claim or apply for. The <a href="/badges">badge overview</a> lists every
    badge and how many participants have earned it.
  </p>
  <ul style="color:var(--muted);max-width:60ch;line-height:1.6;">
    <li>
      <strong>What counts.</strong> On-chain activity (votes, vote rationales,
      registrations, submitted governance actions) and forum activity (posts, topics,
      reactions). Several badges reward doing both: discussing an action in its thread
      and voting on it on-chain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Never the direction of a vote.</strong> No badge depends on voting Yes,
      No, or Abstain. Participation, transparency, and consistency are rewarded;
      positions are not.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tiers.</strong> Count-based badges come in bronze, silver, and gold. The
      badge keeps its motif and changes its color as you reach the next milestone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Permanent.</strong> Once earned, a badge is never taken away, and tiers
      only ever go up.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Where they attach.</strong> On-chain badges belong to the on-chain
      identity (a DRep's badges show on its profile even if it never signed in). Forum
      badges belong to the forum account; for a signed-in DRep both appear together.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hidden badges.</strong> A few badges only reveal their name and criterion
      when earned. They show up as ??? cards until then.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:60ch;line-height:1.6;">
    Awards are recalculated about once an hour from synced on-chain data, so a fresh
    vote can take a little while to show up. Deleted or hidden forum posts never count
    toward badges.
  </p>
</HelpLayout>
